 Very Basic Components
Goal: Understand what a component is
Create a component called Hello.
It should display: Hello, React!
Create a Welcome component.
Show your name inside an <h1> tag.
Create two components:
Header
Footer
Render both inside App.

 Props (Passing Data)
Goal: Learn how components communicate
Create a Greeting component.
Pass a name prop from App.
Display: Hello, <name>
Create a UserCard component.
Props: username, age
Display them in separate <p> tags.
Render the same UserCard component 3 times with different data.

Component Reusability
Goal: Reuse components instead of repeating code
Create a Button component.
It should accept a text prop.
Create a Card component.
Use {children} to display content inside the card.
Wrap different content inside the same Card component.

 Conditional Rendering
Goal: Show or hide components
Create a Status component.
If isOnline is true → show Online
Else → show Offline
Create a Message component.
If no prop is passed, show No messages.

 Lists & Keys
Goal: Render components dynamically
Create an array of names.
Render each name using a NameItem component.
Create a Product component.
Render a list of products using .map().

 Component Structure Practice
Goal: Think in components
Break this UI into components:
[ Header ]
[ Profile ]
[   Avatar ]
[   Name ]
[ Footer ]

Rebuild it using separate components and render them in App.

Bonus Mini Challenges
Create a CounterDisplay component that only displays a number.
Create a Title component that accepts:
text
color
Make a Badge component that shows:
NEW if isNew is true
 Learning Rule (Important)
After each task, ask:
What data does this component need?
Should it come from props or be hardcoded?

